KZ2 patch 6025 (diagnostic): lv2 mutex owner on a timed-out lock, mutexes held at thread exit, PS3_MUTEX_TRACE.

Skipping Killzone 2's intro sometimes paused 17 to 34 s: the main thread's lock helper 0x9F6DB0 takes the movie
stream's mutex with a 0x400000 us timeout and goes on without it when that times out; four to eight such locks timed
out in a row (PS3_SCBLOCK_PROF: syscall 102 blocked 4194 ms, ret 0x8001000B, tid 1). This names the holder: a timed
lock that gives up logs the owner thread and count; a thread that exits while it owns a mutex is logged (lv2 does not
release it), each with the mutex's last eight operations (thread, op, guest lr); PS3_MUTEX_TRACE=<id> logs every lock, trylock, unlock and sys_cond_wait release/re-take of one mutex.
First 24 lines of each kind; nothing else changes.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (hand-merged): sys_mutex.c taken as the patch side whole; upstream's sys_mutex.c changes are #474 (MUTEX_WATCH=2 reporter, POSIX only) and #490 (destroy EBUSY on a held mutex or waiters), the latter part of 6027's destroy rules

